<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6694" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">captātor</span></b> , ōris,
			m.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>one who eagerly reaches after</i>, <i>endeavors
				to obtain</i>, or <i>strives for something</i>
			(rare; not in Cic.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b> only in Prud. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στεφ</span>. 5, 17.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aurae popularis,</span>”
				<i>that courts the popular breeze</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					3, 33, 7</span></i>
			.—Esp., <i>one who hunts after
			legacies</i>, <i>a legacy-hunter</i>, <i><span class="en">Hor. S. 2,
				5, 57</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Petr. 141</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Juv. 5,
			98</span></i>; <i><span class="en">10,
		202</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
